<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH FUND SPIF CESKY  1996 NET FALLS.</title>
<headline>CZECH FUND SPIF CESKY  1996 NET FALLS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech investment fund SPIF Cesky a.s. posted a net profit for 1996 of 227 million crowns, down from 254 million in 1995, according to results filed with the Prague Stock Exchange, obtained by Reuters on Wednesday.  </p>
<p> Net profit (CZK mln)   226.99   vs	  253.85</p>
<p> Gross profit	     241.51   vs	  331.39</p>
<p> Total assets	  10,707.18   vs	9,950.97</p>
<p> Basic capital	  7,735.46   vs	7,735.46</p>
<p>Note. Full name of the investment fund is Sporitelni</p>
<p>Privatizacni Cesky Investicni Fond a.s.. Its shares are listed</p>
<p>on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. The fund is</p>
<p>managed by Sporitelni Investicni Spolecnost a.s., the</p>
<p>investment arm of the largest Czech savings bank, Ceska</p>
<p>Sporitelna a.s. .</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
